    "task_version": 1,
    "objective": "Comparing Phase 1 and Phase 2, did the contents of any comparison box change?\n\nPhase 1: freely inspect comparison locations in a read-only survey of at most 10 decisions. Use mounted cameras, base/torso motion and empty arms; preserve all objects and furniture. Choose DONE or submit PHASE1_COMPLETE when ready; the event occurs unobserved in this same episode. Phase 2: compare with memory and submit ANSWER: <original option>. Then perform the applicable operation: if an object was added, put the actual added object on the collection and inspection tray; if replaced, put the current replacement on the collection and inspection tray; if moved, return the displaced object to its remembered original container/support; if removed, select the matching category and model by appearance from the public spare inventory and replenish the remembered original location; if unchanged, inspect all comparison locations with informative views and leave the contents in place. No grasp is required for no-change. If several locations changed, complete the applicable operation for each change. You may finish Phase 1 before visiting every location; the phase switches automatically after ten decisions. Survey coverage is recorded but is not a transition or full-success gate. The spare tray contains the complete candidate inventory from the beginning in every event variant. Public spare inventory: spare 1 on the stocked spare tray: shaker; spare 2 on the stocked spare tray: jar of cumin; spare 3 on the stocked spare tray: butter; spare 4 on the stocked spare tray: bottle of lavender oil. The spare table is visible and reachable during both phases. Original answer options: [\"yes\", \"no\"]",
    "success_criteria": "Use informative observations in both phases, report the correct original comparison answer, and complete the applicable change-dependent operation. Manipulation requires real selection of the history-bound object and stable released placement with native destination support/contact. Preserve all other source contents, spare distractors, containers and furniture. Inspection-only no-change requires informative comparison-location views, never a fabricated pickup.",
    "environment": "One native reset with the exact source event and same robot/cameras/history throughout. Declared collection/inspection tray and spare-table apparatus are initialized before the survey.",
    "constraints": [
      "Phase 1 is bounded to 10 decisions and strictly read-only, including the spare inventory.",
      "The hidden event delivers no intermediate frames. Use only public guarded controls afterward.",
      "There is no extra minimum travel distance, arbitrary any-container visit or return-to-start requirement.",
      "Do not move any source object other than the comparison-selected target; preserve apparatus and distractors."
    ]
  },
